try":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-62.09040103,45.3736996],[-61.94900232,45.39410049],[-61.72999929,45.48680108],[-61.73307061,45.5024514],[-61.73749938,45.52500128],[-61.50310164,45.62210123],[-61.43718616,45.64925112],[-61.42535206,45.64934733],[-61.48200004,45.71176598],[-61.5326461,45.74842815],[-61.59699347,45.73219891],[-61.70794676,45.68272135],[-61.82134145,45.72022484],[-61.85496466,45.83042012],[-61.82808371,45.88497934],[-61.86829227,45.92106978],[-61.93249191,45.93795612],[-62.010059,45.91570677],[-62.1193057,45.8322941],[-62.19913255,45.80598849],[-62.25807308,45.77129496],[-62.23628818,45.7225972],[-62.23539753,45.72165505],[-62.21795438,45.68006552],[-62.09040103,45.3736996]]]},"properties":{"alert_code":"SPS","alert_type":"statement","alert_name_en":"special weather statement","alert_name_fr":"bulletin m\u00e9t\u00e9orologique sp\u00e9cial","alert_short_name_en":"Special weather","alert_short_name_fr":"M\u00e9t\u00e9orologique sp\u00e9cial","publication_datetime":"2026-11-13T08:28:25.059Z","expiration_datetime":"2026-11-13T23:03:25.059Z","validity_datetime":"2026-11-13T08:24:00.000Z","event_end_datetime":"2026-11-13T21:00:00.000Z","alert_text_en":"The first notable snowfall of the season is expected  for inland areas and over higher terrain.\n\nLocations: parts of mainland Nova Scotia and Cape Breton.\n\nPotential snowfall: possibly reaching 5 cm.\n\nTime span: this morning until this afternoon.\n\nRemarks: A mix of snow and rain is forecast today with some inland areas of Nova Scotia accumulating possibly up to 5 cm of snowfall by this afternoon. Coastal areas will see precipitation fall mainly as rain. There is also a slight risk of freezing rain inland this morning.\n\nSnow and ice accumulation may make travel slow or hazardous. Roads and walkways could become slippery and difficult to navigate. \n\nConsider adjusting travel plans to avoid the most hazardous conditions.\n\nPlease continue to monitor alerts and forecasts issued by Environment Canada. To report severe weather, send an email to NSstorm@ec.gc.ca or post reports on social media using #NSStorm.","alert_text_fr":"La premi\u00e8re importante chute de neige de la saison est pr\u00e9vue pour les secteurs de l'int\u00e9rieur et en terrain montagneux.\n\nR\u00e9gions : certaines parties de la p\u00e9ninsule de la Nouvelle-\u00c9cosse et du Cap-Breton.\n\nAccumulation de neige possible : jusqu'\u00e0 5 cm.\n\nP\u00e9riode : ce matin et cet apr\u00e8s-midi.\n\nRemarques : on pr\u00e9voit un m\u00e9lange de neige et de pluie aujourd'hui, et certaines r\u00e9gions de l'int\u00e9rieur de la Nouvelle-\u00c9cosse pourraient recevoir jusqu'\u00e0 5 cm de neige d'ici cet apr\u00e8s-midi. Dans les r\u00e9gions c\u00f4ti\u00e8res, les pr\u00e9cipitations tomberont surtout sous forme de pluie. Il y a aussi un faible risque de pluie vergla\u00e7ante \u00e0 l'int\u00e9rieur des terres ce matin.\n\nL'accumulation de neige et de verglas pourrait rendre les d\u00e9placements lents ou dangereux. La circulation risque de devenir difficile sur les routes et les trottoirs, possiblement glissants.\n\nSongez \u00e0 modifier vos projets de d\u00e9placements afin d'\u00e9viter les conditions les plus dangereuses.\n\nVeuillez continuer \u00e0 surveiller les alertes et les pr\u00e9visions \u00e9mises par Environnement Canada. Pour signaler du temps violent, envoyez un courriel \u00e0 meteoNS@ec.gc.ca ou publiez un message sur les r\u00e9seaux sociaux en utilisant #NSMeteo.","risk_colour_en":null,"risk_colour_fr":null,"confidence_en":null,"confidence_fr":null,"impact_en":null,"impact_fr":null,"feature_name_en":"Antigonish County","feature_name_fr":"comt\u00e9 d'Antigonish","province":"NS","status_en":"continued","status_fr":"maintenu","feature_id":"fea1-802"}}],"numberMatched":199,"numberReturned":3,"links":[{"type":"application/geo+json","rel":"self","title":"This document as GeoJSON","href":"https://api.weather.gc.ca/collections/weather-alerts/items?f=json&limit=3"},{"rel"